  {
   "id": "mZzpihh42rsJ",
   "from": "Yihui Xie",
   "author": "85e053d519f0f372",
   "date": "2014-07-16T21:03:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: packrat::init() fails with error in findLocalRepoForPkg",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "FYI, here is how R core checks dependencies:\r<br><a href=\"https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/trunk/src/library/tools/R/QC.R#L5195\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/trunk/src/library/tools/R/QC.R%23L5195&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793242831375000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0qEinRi6Od25Hj6sjR4QuE\">https://github.com/wch/r-source/blob/trunk/src/library/tools/R/QC.R#L5195</a>\r<br>\r<br>Because I know this, sometimes I intentionally use something like\r<br>(function(pkg) library(pkg, character.only = TRUE))(&quot;foo&quot;) to silence\r<br>R CMD check and cheat when I (optionally) need a package but do not\r<br>want CRAN maintainers to know it :-p\r<br>\r<br>Regards,\r<br>Yihui\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On Wed, Jul 16, 2014 at 3:42 PM, Kevin Ushey &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ke...@rstudio.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Awesome, thanks! I think we should be fixing our dependency inference for\r<br>&gt; things like this as well.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Wed, Jul 16, 2014 at 1:39 PM, Harlan Harris &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">har...@harris.name</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Hi, no, I can&#39;t share the project. But your note helped me figure it out.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; It seems like packrat is doing a search for &quot;library&quot; and &quot;require&quot; in any\r<br>&gt;&gt; R file in any subdirectory. That explained why Rcmdr was getting loaded --\r<br>&gt;&gt; it&#39;s in an &quot;old/&quot; directory.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; From there, I figure out that you&#39;re doing some sort of regexes or\r<br>&gt;&gt; something to find packages to include. I&#39;ve got a tricky bit in one file\r<br>&gt;&gt; that I figured out was causing you to look for &quot;pkg&quot;:\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; require_all &lt;- function(pkg_list) {\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;   rets &lt;- sapply(pkg_list, function(pkg)\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; suppressPackageStartupMessages(require(pkg, character.only=TRUE,\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; quietly=TRUE)))\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;   if (!all(rets)) stop(&quot;Failed to load packages: &quot;, paste(pkg_list[rets],\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; collapse=&quot;, &quot;))\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; }\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; require_all(c(&quot;rmarkdown&quot;, &quot;optparse&quot;, &quot;dplyr&quot;, &quot;ggplot2&quot;, &quot;pander&quot;,\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; &quot;data.table&quot;))\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; If I comment that out, it inits OK. Too much cleverness, I guess!\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; I&#39;ll make the above simpler and get rid of my old files, and see how it\r<br>&gt;&gt; goes.\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; Thank you!\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt; On Wed, Jul 16, 2014 at 4:07 PM, Kevin Ushey &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ke...@rstudio.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Hi Harlan,\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Any chance you can share the project (e.g. is it on GitHub)? I am\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; wondering why a package named &#39;pkg&#39; is being picked up.\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Kevin\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; On Wednesday, July 16, 2014 12:56:55 PM UTC-7, Harlan Harris wrote:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Hi. I&#39;ve got a small project I developed in RStudio, and I&#39;d like to\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; move it over to Packrat. Following the instructions, I&#39;ve installed v\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 0.3.0.105, along with devtools 1.5. However, I&#39;m getting this:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &gt; packrat::init()\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Initializing packrat project in directory:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; - &quot;/home/harlan/Development/risk-model-report&quot;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Error in findLocalRepoForPkg(pkg, repos) :\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;   No package &#39;pkg&#39; found in local repositories specified\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; In addition: Warning messages:\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 1: In readLines(file) :\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;   incomplete final line found on\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; &#39;/home/harlan/Development/risk-model-report/risk-model-report.Rmd&#39;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 2: In FUN(c(&quot;data.table&quot;, &quot;Rcmdr&quot;, &quot;pscl&quot;, &quot;pkg&quot;, &quot;rmarkdown&quot;)[[5L]],  :\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;   Package &#39;pkg&#39; not available in repository or locally\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; 3: In FUN(c(&quot;data.table&quot;, &quot;Rcmdr&quot;, &quot;pscl&quot;, &quot;pkg&quot;, &quot;rmarkdown&quot;)[[5L]],  :\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;   Package &#39;rmarkdown&#39; not available in repository or locally\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt; Any ideas? Thanks!\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;\r<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;  -